        "status": "validated",
        "explanation": null,
        "tags": [],
        "source_refs": [],
        "reference_answer": "CREATE TABLE or ALTER TABLE defines structure, primary keys and a foreign key from Employee.dept_id to Department.dept_id. INSERT adds rows, UPDATE changes existing values and DELETE removes rows. A salary update uses a predicate identifying intended employees; omitting WHERE can update every row. A referenced department deletion is rejected unless its declared referential action permits it; do not assume cascading deletion. These are conceptual answers: learner sandbox execution accepts only read-only SELECT and rolls back, so it cannot run DML/DDL.",
